WEBVTT

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.820
Is he here?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.870
S-Camera, standby.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.170
So, Mr. Director, how does it feel to be nominated for an Oscar?

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.420
Not bad at all.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.220
But I still haven't won anything yet.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.050
It's still an honor, however.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.560
There are rumors that you got a big star for your next project.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.850
That would be great, but I wouldn't say that as of yet.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.650
But it's true that we've made a few offers.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.320
Be careful. If he notices then it's curtains for us.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.840
Get a close-up! Get in as close as you can!

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.060
Hey... did he just...?

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.230
Relax, these state-of-the-art super telephoto lenses were developed by NASA.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.820
To him we're just a tiny blip on the horizon.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.740
Sir, is there something wrong?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.320
No, it's nothing.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.830
All right, that's a wrap.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.840
Thus begins our one-of-a-kind film.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.090
A film the likes no one has seen before.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.260
<i>So the dice has been rolled, huh?</i>

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.900
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.030
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:26.500
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.040
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.670
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:42.100
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.560
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:52.860
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.150
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.240
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:08.330
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.920
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.300
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:24.510
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.810
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:34.860
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:52.420
Casting

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.140
All right, let's do this!

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.470
Scene 17, take one!

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.600
And... Action!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.690
So you deceived me!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.990
I've had it. I'm fed up with pushy women like you!

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.240
Please... don't leave me!

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.910
I told you, we're through!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.960
Cut!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:40.300
Hey, can't you speed up the ins and outs a little?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.420
And we didn't have enough focus near the middle.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.720
Lower the key lights a little!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.640
We're getting some weird shadows under their noses during the close-ups!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.270
Let's make this last cut count!

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.520
Nice work, Jean.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.770
That look on your face when you rose from the floor will convince any hit man take a job.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.320
Be sure to maintain that expression if you want this thing to look real.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.990
I know, Eric.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:09.370
Still, this script. It's so similar to my past that it's scary.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:42.150
You've read up on that scenario, Eric?

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:47.910
This here's the sponsor of the movie we've commissioned from you.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.790
I can't tell you his name for various reasons.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:59.580
So let's start talking about the
movie all of us are going to make.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.680
We have two conditions you must meet in producing this film.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:13.560
First is the scenario. It has already been completed.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.640
We won't be allowing any changes.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.100
And the other condition?

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.150
The casting.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.480
So, this contract killer hired by the woman...

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.070
We will be using a real one, of course.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.660
A professional that is at the very top in his field.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.120
But, if we do that...

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.830
Yes, the man playing the leading part will die like it says in the script.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:43.380
Well, at least you've noticed how marvelous this project is.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:52.140
We will be distributing an altered script to your staff and cast that leaves out the ending.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:59.440
That means there will be an incident involving the real live hit man during the last part.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.480
It's an incident that is not in the script.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.690
It will be a movie no one has ever commissioned before.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:14.160
Once it's complete, our company
will handle the global distribution.

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:18.200
Make no mistake, this will be the world's biggest hit.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.920
So, this top ranked contract killer we're talking about...?

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.460
This man.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:28.880
Got it, you'll be hiring this man.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.220
However, he must not know that he's in a movie.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.100
He must think this is the real thing, not a movie, Jean.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:40.940
I got it.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.400
I've gotten in touch with that agent.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.200
It looks like it'll be 7:00 tonight.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.930
A woman called wanting to meet at 7:00 tonight in order to hire you.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:16.350
Leave it right there.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.010
Uh, right!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.780
How's the reception on the hidden mike?

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.370
Just peachy. We can hear her anywhere inside the city.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:46.920
The phone's ringing.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.630
Hello?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:58.050
Pick up a taxi in front of your apartment in twenty minutes.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.180
And then, uh-

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.230
Have the infrared camera on standby!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.480
We're gonna be capturing the taxi stopping in front of Jean's apartment in 20 minutes!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.610
All right.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.860
It's now or never.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.940
Don't push it, camera people!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.860
If he sees us, it's all over.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.190
Maintain your distance as you shadow them!

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:55.900
Roger that.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:10:00.450
Um, I was only told to ride this taxi.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.950
Shall we discuss the job?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.580
So that means... you're...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.130
That's right.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.210
That's a great voice.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:14.920
A voice of a star!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.440
...that was how Paul... Paul Dominic betrayed me.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.450
I can still forgive him for leaving me.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.290
What I can't forgive is what he did after that.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:52.290
I begged him again and again to see me but he never responds.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.130
Instead he just sends me a $500,000 check.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.680
It's like... he's telling me how much I'm worth.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.970
Nice work, Jean.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.890
She's amazingly intense just as the script calls for.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:09.230
To Jean, this is <i>not</i>  an act.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.940
This is the real deal.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.780
Golgo must not find out we're doing this to make a movie.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:25.080
That's why we chose a no-name actress named Jean Barbara.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.040
Which means...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.960
You can't bluff a top level professional.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:37.300
No matter how good the act is, Golgo will see through it.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.340
Jean Barbara shares a similar history as her character.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.390
She does?

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:46.100
Mm-hmm.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:52.350
She was betrayed by a guy and actually hired a hit man to rub him out.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.150
A go-between...

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.110
...told me that you never take a job for five hundred grand.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:04.820
But... that's all I have. Moreover...

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:10.000
It would mean a lot to me to hire you and kill him with the same $500,000 he sent me!

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.750
Please, Mr. Togo.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:14.630
Say that you'll accept!

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.590
This is where the hit man gives his consent...

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:24.720
Not good.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.050
He'll suspect something if there's too much silence.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:44.780
Back when he was still an unknown actor

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:47.370
I never stopped devoting my all to him.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.200
Way to go, Jean! Get him with your ad-libbing!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.880
Even when he injured his dominant left
hand in an accident, I was there for him!

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.090
But once he became a big star, he...

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.090
This is bad.

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.390
She's not going by the script.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.310
What?

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.640
If we don't need them, we'll just cut them out later.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:17.230
As long she's able to get our main man Golgo to consent...

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.980
Please!

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.740
End my bitterness!

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.450
All right. I accept.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.990
Yes!

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:36.250
Paul should be at the San Diego Golf
Course tomorrow. You can get him then.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.130
Sure.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:43.340
So you'll make him choke on his $500,000 tomorrow, right?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.630
Make him feel my misery?

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.480
All right... cut!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.140
It's all on here, Eric!

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:58.600
We got him.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.270
Hook, line and sinker!

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.290
So he accepted?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.540
Yeah.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.160
No need to worry.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.380
Once he accepts a job, he lets nothing stand in his way of his completing it.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:25.010
As long as the client doesn't break his rules.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:33.510
We've made some prognostications based on past patterns he employs.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:15:00.080
That golf course is a perfect place to take a shot without nobody seeing you.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.710
So the target will be on the green at the 15th hole

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:07.130
and he'll be taking his shot from within the woods in the rear.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.340
You can bet the farm that Golgo will be right there tomorrow.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:19.600
That is where his life as a sniper will come to an end.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:24.610
The man who screwed over countless people.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:06.230
Eric, are you sure about filming Paul on his day off?

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:12.400
This is not even in the script. Shouldn't we be following our contract killer?

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.030
Thomas's crew is taking care of that.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:16.030
Don't sweat it.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.500
Well, if you say.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:24.540
<i>It's almost time for the moment of
the century. You'd better capture it!</i>

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:25.920
Understood.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:29.550
He's there just as anticipated.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:53.820
Be sure to stay on Paul!

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:57.320
I don't see how this footage will be of much use.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.200
Just stay on him!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:04.460
I want you to film Paul while he
still doesn't know he's on camera.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:07.130
Fine, fine, you got it.

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.450
<i>What's the deal, Golgo 13?</i>

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.160
<i>Hurry up and shoot him!</i>

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.850
Why aren't you shooting him?!

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:00.760
Huh?

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:33.750
What is this?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:34.840
Why are you...?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.300
Paul must have been born right-handed.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:42.100
That did not look like he was forced to be right-handed.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:50.730
<i>Even when he injured his dominant left
hand in an accident, I was there for him!</i>

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:56.570
I thought I kept my cool back then, but I guess I still had the jitters.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:01.240
The man I once had in my real life was left-handed.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.910
For me to mix him up with Paul...

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.830
The director's bound to give me an earful.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:07.950
I see.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.830
So you were just an actress?

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:17.920
You're going to tell me everything you know.

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.970
W-What?

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:21.800
Don't start throwing out false accusations-!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.390
Talk!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.810
All right, fine!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.390
Besides you're doing this because you're after my body, right?

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.400
I'll give it to you, you didn't have to be rough.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.420
She's dead... he killed Jean!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.250
Impossible.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.380
Where the hell did it all go wrong?

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:59.880
This came completely out of nowhere!

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.680
This is bad.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:04.930
If he knows about our movie, then he's...

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:07.890
I'm calling the cops!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:08.890
Wait!

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.100
Start filming.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.150
Preserve the scene in that camera!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.940
You're joking.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.190
Just do it, dammit!

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.240
I'll make it my own.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:28.200
I'll make this movie my own, despite all this!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:31.960
Let's go!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.470
Hurry!

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.850
What are you planning to do, Eric?

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:53.230
All the data we filmed are right here.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:58.320
As long as I have this... I can make a movie anywhere.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:33.100
I see. So we failed.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:36.140
Sorry to say.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:41.190
If we had spread that movie around the world, he would have become an overnight celebrity.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.700
Then the unrelenting public eye would have put a check to his movements.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:55.160
That plan, however roundabout it was, would have taken him out in a way that other professionals have failed.

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.510
It... It can't be!

00:22:03.510 --> 00:22:06.010
Golgo's sniffed out our location?

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:08.590
That man...

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:12.430
So this is the how the movie ends once we casted him?

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:45.760
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:52.970
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:59.060
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:03.900
of flowers.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:11.530
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.120
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:19.500
I had a dream.

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:25.210
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:31.800
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:37.350
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:43.860
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:48.440
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:51.610
I won't.

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:09.460
Ben has stolen Golgo 13's name and used it to contract a job he completed with his knife.

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:15.390
He chases Golgo down to a luxury
liner and becomes part of a show.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:20.520
Then, Ben has Golgo within his sights...

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:25.360
Next time on Golgo 13: Love is a Knife.

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:26.480
Love is a Knife

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:29.530
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
